{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788297753647,"sessionID":"ses_fa1260973ffeOIaNGhvLCc80qv","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8eaf42b1f3475249","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cat justfile"},"output":"# List available recipes.\ndefault:\n    @just --list\n\n# The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\ntest:\n    cargo nextest run\n\n# The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\ncheck:\n    cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'\n\n# Opt-in: run the skipped Euler 8/11/13/18 programs against real puzzle data in DIR, outside\n# `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\neuler-data DIR:\n    EULER_DATA={{DIR}} cargo nextest run --run-ignored ignored-only -E 'test(euler_real_data)'\n\n# Run clippy with the repo's lint set, the same surface the Stop hook checks.\nclippy:\n    cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets\n\n# Formatter check over every .toy file from the repo root down (exit 1 on drift).\nfmt:\n    cargo run -q -- fmt\n\n# Rewrite drifted files in place (same exit code as the check).\nfmt-write:\n    cargo run -q -- fmt --write\n\n# The repo's mechanical checks, the same surface the Stop hook runs.\nchecks:\n    bash .claude/checks/run.sh\n\n# The autonomous drive loop: a tick every 600s, live colorized output, Ctrl-C to stop. Run ONE.\ndrive:\n    .claude/scripts/drive-loop.sh\n\n# Fire one coordinator tick right now (zero tokens if there is nothing to do).\ntick:\n    .claude/scripts/drive-tick.sh\n\n# Watch the current coordinator tick live (detaches with Ctrl-C, tick untouched).\npeek:\n    .claude/scripts/tick-peek.sh\n","metadata":{"output":"# List available recipes.\ndefault:\n    @just --list\n\n# The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\ntest:\n    cargo nextest run\n\n# The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\ncheck:\n    cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'\n\n# Opt-in: run the skipped Euler 8/11/13/18 programs against real puzzle data in DIR, outside\n# `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\neuler-data DIR:\n    EULER_DATA={{DIR}} cargo nextest run --run-ignored ignored-only -E 'test(euler_real_data)'\n\n# Run clippy with the repo's lint set, the same surface the Stop hook checks.\nclippy:\n    cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets\n\n# Formatter check over every .toy file from the repo root down (exit 1 on drift).\nfmt:\n    cargo run -q -- fmt\n\n# Rewrite drifted files in place (same exit code as the check).\nfmt-write:\n    cargo run -q -- fmt --write\n\n# The repo's mechanical checks, the same surface the Stop hook runs.\nchecks:\n    bash .claude/checks/run.sh\n\n# The autonomous drive loop: a tick every 600s, live colorized output, Ctrl-C to stop. Run ONE.\ndrive:\n    .claude/scripts/drive-loop.sh\n\n# Fire one coordinator tick right now (zero tokens if there is nothing to do).\ntick:\n    .claude/scripts/drive-tick.sh\n\n# Watch the current coordinator tick live (detaches with Ctrl-C, tick untouched).\npeek:\n    .claude/scripts/tick-peek.sh\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cat justfile","time":{"start":1788297753637,"end":1788297753645}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The branch is behind origin/main by 116 commits. Interesting. But I'm told to work only inside this worktree and not push. Let me check what the current state is. Wait, the task says \"Fresh start: the previous run died at startup and produced nothing\". So I should treat this as clean.\n\nBut branch is behind main by 116 commits. Hmm. Let me check the justfile and understand the tasks. Let me also check if there's a scratchpad active. Let me check.\n\nActually, the branch is behind origin/main. This is a worktree on issue-149. The task says work only inside this worktree. Let me not worry about the branch being behind for now - the issue says implement Float per ADR 0007.\n\nWait, but there might be prior work on this branch. Let me check the git log more and see if there's a scratchpad.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05eda30de001fvEBk1oDsuowhH","sessionID":"ses_fa1260973ffeOIaNGhvLCc80qv","messageID":"msg_05eda22640017ESqVZ1S9RoOO2"}}
